%% OutboxRelay.pollOnce / claimAndDispatch / recordFailure as implemented in
%% apps/api/src/platform/outbox/outbox.relay.ts. Handlers are registered from
%% modules/ (outbox-bindings.ts registers AuditLogHandler); the relay never knows event types.
sequenceDiagram
    participant Timer as setInterval<br/>(OUTBOX_POLL_INTERVAL_MS, default 1000)
    participant Relay as OutboxRelay<br/>(platform/outbox)
    participant DB as PostgreSQL
    participant Handler as OutboxHandler<br/>(e.g. AuditLogHandler)

    Note over Timer,Relay: Started on bootstrap except when NODE_ENV=test.<br/>A rejected poll is logged, never left unhandled.<br/>A poll still running makes the next tick return at once.
    Timer->>Relay: pollOnce()
    Relay->>DB: BEGIN (UnitOfWork.withTransaction)

    Relay->>DB: SELECT id, aggregate_type, aggregate_id, event_type, org_id, payload, occurred_at, attempts<br/>FROM outbox_events<br/>WHERE status = 'pending' AND (next_attempt_at IS NULL OR next_attempt_at <= now())<br/>ORDER BY id LIMIT $1 (OUTBOX_BATCH_SIZE, default 20, max 64)<br/>FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED
    Note over DB: The claim is the row lock, not a status update.<br/>A second relay polling now skips these rows and claims others.
    DB-->>Relay: claimed rows (possibly none)

    loop each claimed event, in id order
        Relay->>DB: SAVEPOINT outbox_event
        alt a handler is registered for event_type and succeeds
            Relay->>Handler: handle(tx, event)
            Handler->>DB: INSERT INTO audit_log (...) ON CONFLICT (event_id) DO NOTHING
            Relay->>DB: UPDATE outbox_events SET status = 'processed', processed_at = now() WHERE id = $1
            Relay->>DB: RELEASE SAVEPOINT outbox_event
        else no handler, a JS error, or an SQL error in the handler
            Note over Relay,DB: An SQL error aborts every later statement on the connection<br/>until something rolls back. The savepoint is that rollback point.<br/>An unregistered type fails with "No outbox handler registered for event type ...".
            Relay->>DB: ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT outbox_event (undoes only this handler's writes)
            alt attempts + 1 >= OUTBOX_MAX_ATTEMPTS (default 8)
                Relay->>DB: UPDATE outbox_events SET status = 'dead', attempts = $2,<br/>last_error = $3, next_attempt_at = NULL WHERE id = $1
                Note over Relay: Leaves the pending predicate, so it never blocks later events.<br/>Visible to ops_admin at GET /ops/outbox.
            else retry later
                Relay->>DB: UPDATE outbox_events SET attempts = $2, last_error = $3,<br/>next_attempt_at = now() + backoff WHERE id = $1
                Note over Relay: backoff = min(200 ms × 2^(attempts-1), 30 s), ±25% jitter
            end
        end
    end

    Relay->>DB: COMMIT
    Note over DB: Processed, retried and dead events are all recorded in one commit.<br/>The row locks are released.<br/>A crash before COMMIT rolls everything back: events return to pending<br/>with attempts unchanged, and a handler's write is undone with them.
    Relay-->>Timer: { claimed, processed, failed, dead }
